  "notes": "Cash basis county, governmental funds only. Statement lines from the Total Governmental Funds column (p4); beginning/ending cash are the cash basis fund balances the statement rolls forward (equal to cash, p3). Proceeds from Sale of Bonds 3,675,000 (Highway Allocation Bond Repay Fund) printed under other financing sources -> debt_proceeds; that fund's principal payments 4,400,437 are recorded as printed. Taxes 4,674,607 kept as one line (no printed breakdown by tax type); in detail the Inheritance Fund's Taxes 527,940 are inheritance tax by fund name. Balance sheet from the governmental funds Statement of Cash Basis Assets and Fund Balances (p3), totals equal the Statement of Net Position (p1). Detail: General Fund budget schedule (pp5-6, departments not itemized), Road, Inheritance and Highway Allocation Bond Repay budget schedules (pp7-8); the one-line Inheritance disbursements take the function and the Highway Allocation Bond Repay disbursements 4,412,172 are split into principal/interest from that fund's column on p4. Nonmajor funds: the combining statement has 10 fund columns (pp12-13), so its Total Nonmajor Funds column is used; the one-line per-fund nonmajor budget schedules (pp9-11) are not recorded to avoid double counting. Read pages 1-13 of 13"
}
